      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيَاطٌ</span></b> : see 1, throughout the greater part of
the latter half of the paragraph. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيْنَهُمَا مُمَايَطَةٌ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُهَايَطَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَايَطَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُسَايَطَةٌ</span> are said to
signify <i>Between them two is low, faint,</i> or <i>gentle,
speaking.</i> (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هيط</span>.)

